@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+id: 2026-10-08-auth-workflow-boundaries
+title: Preserve explicit authentication and membership workflows
+priority: high
+area: auth
+type: security
+delivery: code-patch
+intent: >
+  Mark User.twoFactorEnabled and User.twoFactorMethod CRUD-read-only and regenerate
+  the complete API and SDK artifacts. Stored two-factor secrets and recovery codes remain
+  GraphQL-omitted; add the omission where a project has lost it. Keep their readable output fields and the explicit
+  two-factor setup, verification and disable workflows. When removing an organization member,
+  constrain the delete by the selected membership ID, target user ID and organization ID after
+  acquiring the account lock. Keep the existing owner-removal guard atomic by excluding the owner
+  role in the write predicate. A changed membership must fail without deleting its new assignment
+  or a newly promoted owner.
+why: >
+  Authentication settings and organization changes retain their application workflow boundaries
+  across administrative and concurrent writes. Details will follow in a coordinated advisory.
+affectedPaths:
+  - libs/api/prisma/src/lib/schemas/schema.prisma
+  - libs/api/custom/src/lib/default/organization/organization.service.ts
+  - apps/api-e2e/src/auth/auth-crud-invariants.spec.ts
+  - apps/api-e2e/src/auth/auth-crud-concurrency.spec.ts
+packageReleases: []
+verification:
+  - pnpm exec nx run api-custom:test
+  - pnpm exec nx run api-e2e:test
+  - pnpm exec nx run-many -t lint typecheck
+agentHints:
+  - Run full generation; never hand-edit generated DTOs or SDK types.
+  - Preserve the project's explicit two-factor workflows and membership authorization policies.
+  - There is no database migration and normal rolling deployment is supported.
